From: PW4 Android port
Subject: [PW4] Bluetooth: headphones whose own connection fails are called back

On the PW4 the A2DP source offers SBC alone (device/amazon/pw4 Bluetooth
overlay, Jump 56): AAC costs the single 1 GHz core more than it has to give
while WeRead turns pages. Headphones that connect on their own -- switched on
next to the Kindle, or after the Kindle wakes -- may configure AAC, and once
that is refused (btif_av "Received BTA_AV_REJECT_EVT", a2dp_codec "cannot find
codec configuration for peer OTA codec AAC") some never try SBC: rc2 on
2026-11-27, a pair of 夜鹰 headphones, two attempts both lost, while a tap in
Settings connected at once, because an outgoing connection lets this side
pick the codec.

So an incoming connection that fails while pending is made again from this
side, 2 s later, once per device in 10 s, and only for a bonded device whose
A2DP priority is above PRIORITY_OFF. A device that connected meanwhile makes
the call a no-op (Connected ignores CONNECT for its own device).

